  "author_association": "NONE",
  "body": "### ESLint version\n\n10.8.1\n\n### What problem do you want to solve?\n\nCan the following please be added to the recommended config:\n\n```\ncurly: ['error', 'multi-line'],\n'no-useless-rename': 'error',\n'object-shorthand': 'error',\n'prefer-template': 'error',\n```\n\nI believe these to be non controversial rules that all result in shorter, more readable and more performant code, so should therefore be recommended approaches. The exception is perhaps the `curly` rule, which is maybe more of a visual preference, but it does enforce formatting consistency between conditional statements and other code blocks like functions and switch statements that use curly brackets.\n\n### What do you think is the correct solution?\n\nUpdating the recommended config\n\n### Participation\n\n- [x] I am willing to submit a pull request for this change.\n\n### AI acknowledgment\n\n- [ ] I did not use AI to generate this issue report.\n- [ ] (If the above is not checked) I have reviewed the AI-generated content before submitting.\n\n### Additional comments\n\n_No response_",
